          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              From
              %a{:href => "product+of+simplices#CartesianProductOfSimplicialSetsIsComponentwise"} this Prop.
              it is clear (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "product+of+simplices#DegenerateSimplicesInProductOfSimplicialSets"} this Remark
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \,\colon\, \Delta[p+q] \xrightarrow{\;} \Delta[p] \times \Delta[q]
              is degenerate precisely if, when regarded as a path as above, it contains a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
              step, i.e. one which moves neither horizontally nor vertically. But then — by degree reasons, since we are looking at paths of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p + q
              steps in a lattice of side length
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              — it must be that the path proceeds by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo +
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p + q
              unit steps.
          %h3#nerve_of_the_inertia_groupoid Nerve of the inertia groupoid
          %p
            Some basic facts about the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of an
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inertia+groupoid"} inertia groupoid
          %p
          #InertiaGroupoidOfDeloopingGroupoidIsAdjointActionGroupoid.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inertia+groupoid"} inertia groupoid
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"} delooping groupoid
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              %br/
              The inertia groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda \mathbf{B} G
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint action
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              on itself:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi ad
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi G
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                      %munderover
                        %mo ⇉
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Ad
                            %mrow
