                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DerivedDegreeShiftAdjunction"} (7)
                %p
                  (observing that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complexes"} normalized chain complexes
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+simplicial+abelian+groups"} free simplicial abelian groups
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
                  representative of the correct
                  = succeed "-image" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}(-)
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_\bullet
                  are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functors"} left Quillen functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo +
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ch_+, \otimes)
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
                  (
                  %a{:href => "model+structure+on+chain+complexes#ProjectiveModelStructureOnConnectiveChainComplexesIsMonoidal"}> this Prop.
                  ), so that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \oplus \mathbb{Z}[1]
                  is the correct
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
              %li
                %p
                  the ninth line is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
                  onto the second
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct summand
              %li
                %p
                  the last line is Def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupoidCohomology"}
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+cohomology"} groupoid cohomology
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram+chase"} Chasing
              a group cocycle (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupCohomology"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FormOfTheSimplicialEvaluationMap"}
              when it gets sent through the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber+map"} Eilenberg-Zilber map
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SumFormulaForTransgressedCocycle"} (3)
              to be proven.
            %p
              Hence it only remains to see that this concrete composite
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TransgressionDecomposed"} (12)
              is equal to the abstractly defined transgression map (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Transgression"}
            %p#VerifyingTheMapIsCorrect
              This follows by Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeLoopSpaceOfEMSpaceIdentifiedViaEilenbergZilber"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo +
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[n] \in Ch_+
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+object"} fibrant object
                  (like every object in the projective
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+connective+chain+complexes"} model structure on connective chain complexes
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi W
